### 2026-09-08 — V5 rulebook sync, Phase 2 (Core Influence parity, Standing, recovery reference)

Completed the audit's Phase 2. `coreInfluence` entries in `actor-combatant.mjs` now carry
`severity`/`condition` fields exactly like `coreWounds` (previously just `{filled}`), filled in the
same fixed 5-slot order (2 Light, 2 Serious, 1 Critical) with a generated label like "Light Injury"
— the Influence equivalent of a Wound Condition, same canon gap noted for Wounds (no named
mechanical effect per severity exists yet, descriptive only). Added a `standing` derived getter in
`prepareDerivedData()` reading off the same count-based thresholds as `woundState`
(0=Undamaged, 1-2=Light Injury, 3-4=Serious Injury, 5=Critical Injury) — this is a real design
inference, not something spelled out verbatim in the rules text: the Standing-by-Injury-State table
in part-v-social-encounters.md never states its counting rule explicitly, but Core Influence uses
"the same five-box severity track as Core Wounds" with an identical 2/2/1 severity distribution and
the same four narrative-state count, so mirroring Wound State's exact thresholds was the
