### 2026-09-09 — Surge rule reverted: Success Die excluded from Surge count again

The 2026-09-08 "every 6+ die including the Success Die earns a Surge" change (see that date's
entry above) was itself wrong — the user clarified the actual ordering is "successes come AFTER
the Defense has been met": the Success Die is spent meeting Defense, and only the OTHER dice
showing 6+ grant a Surge. Worked example given: 8, 6, 6 against Defense 5 — the 8 succeeds and
earns no Surge, only the two 6s do (2 Surges, not 3). Reverted `resolveCombatRoll()`
(`module/dice/essence-roll.mjs`) to exclude `successDieIndex` from the Surge sum, updated its
doc comment and `roll-card.hbs`'s dice-face styling (a die can no longer be both `success-die` and
`surge-die`, so the CSS's now-dead 3-class combined rule in `essence.css` was removed rather than
left to bit-rot). v0.6.43, see CHANGELOG.md.

**New, not previously modeled**: an "open" roll — the dice-commit dialog's existing "leave blank
to roll open" option, when a target's Defense isn't known or hasn't been declared — should not
auto-resolve a spendable Surge total, since there's no Defense to count "after." `rollEssencePool()`
now computes `openRoll = !multi && defense == null` and the chat card swaps the normal Surge/spend
UI for a plain "GM decides" note listing the candidate 6+ dice, instead of presenting a number the
system can't actually justify. This only applies to single-target rolls with no declared Defense —
multi-target rolls still have per-target Defenses even though the shared roll's own `defense` param
is null for a different reason (each target is resolved independently), so `openRoll` explicitly
excludes the `multi` case.

